<figcaption class="small-efficiency-figure-caption"><span class="se-cap" data-se-cap="flops" data-figure-number="2a">Performance-Compute Comparison. Sweeping <a href="/news/introducing-inkling/#controllable-thinking-effort">reasoning effort</a> from <a href="https://tinker-docs.thinkingmachines.ai/cookbook/inkling/thinking-effort/">minimal to xhigh</a> traces the performance-compute curve (output TFLOPs per sample) for Inkling-Small and Inkling on Terminal-Bench 2.1, HLE (no tool), and IFBench. We show that Inkling-Small is competitive with other open-weights models in a similar size range on both performance and efficiency. Output TFLOPs per sample are estimated as 2 × active parameters × mean generated tokens per sample, where generated-token counts include reasoning tokens and come from our evaluations or public reports from <a href="https://artificialanalysis.ai/evaluations/">Artificial Analysis</a>.</span><span class="se-cap" data-se-cap="cost" data-figure-number="2b" hidden>Performance-Cost Comparison. Sweeping <a href="https://thinkingmachines.ai/news/introducing-inkling/#controllable-thinking-effort">reasoning effort</a> from <a href="https://tinker-docs.thinkingmachines.ai/cookbook/inkling/thinking-effort/">minimal to xhigh</a> traces the performance-cost curve (dollar output price per sample) for Inkling-Small and Inkling on Terminal-Bench 2.1, HLE (no tool), and IFBench. We show that Inkling-Small is competitive with other open-weights models in a similar size range on both performance and efficiency. Estimated output cost per sample is computed as mean generated tokens per sample × output price per token, where generated-token counts include reasoning tokens and come from our evaluations or public reports from <a href="https://artificialanalysis.ai/evaluations/">Artificial Analysis</a> (reasoning + answer tokens only). Inkling output pricing is $4.05 / 1M tokens and Inkling-Small output pricing is $1.20 / 1M tokens; for comparison-model pricing, we use the model provider’s official pricing when possible. When this is not possible, we use pricing from the recommended third party inference provider or pricing from Artificial Analysis, whichever is lower.</span></figcaption>
<script>
(function () {
  var fig = document.currentScript.closest("[data-se-switch]");
  if (!fig) return;
  var tablist = fig.querySelector('[role="tablist"]');
  var tabs = fig.querySelectorAll("[data-se-tab]");
  var panels = fig.querySelectorAll("[data-se-panel]");
  var caps = fig.querySelectorAll("[data-se-cap]");
  function indicator() {
    var active = tablist.querySelector('[aria-selected="true"]');
    if (!active) return;
    var lr = tablist.getBoundingClientRect(), tr = active.getBoundingClientRect();
    if (!tr.width) return;
    tablist.classList.add("demo-tabs-enhanced");
    tablist.style.setProperty("--demo-tab-width", tr.width.toFixed(2) + "px");
    tablist.style.setProperty("--demo-tab-height", tr.height.toFixed(2) + "px");
    tablist.style.setProperty("--demo-tab-x", (tr.left - lr.left).toFixed(2) + "px");
    tablist.style.setProperty("--demo-tab-y", (tr.top - lr.top).toFixed(2) + "px");
    tablist.style.setProperty("--demo-tab-indicator-opacity", "1");
  }
  function show(which) {
    tabs.forEach(function (t) { var s = t.getAttribute("data-se-tab") === which; t.setAttribute("aria-selected", s ? "true" : "false"); t.tabIndex = s ? 0 : -1; });
    panels.forEach(function (p) { p.hidden = p.getAttribute("data-se-panel") !== which; });
    caps.forEach(function (c) { c.hidden = c.getAttribute("data-se-cap") !== which; });
    indicator();
  }
  tabs.forEach(function (t) { t.addEventListener("click", function () { show(t.getAttribute("data-se-tab")); }); });
  requestAnimationFrame(indicator);
  window.addEventListener("load", indicator);
  window.addEventListener("resize", indicator);
})();
</script>
</figure>
<p>We are releasing the <a href="https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small">full weights</a> of Inkling-Small. We’re also making it available for fine-tuning on Tinker, and for text, image, and audio chat on <a href="https://tinker.thinkingmachines.ai/playground?utm_source=blog&amp;utm_campaign=inkling_small_model_release">Tinker Playground</a>.</p>
<h2 id="capabilities">Capabilities</h2>
<p>As we build our model family, we are always iterating on our approach. Inkling-Small began training after its larger counterpart, which let us improve its training process. For example, we made changes to Inkling-Small’s pre-training data mix and machine learning recipe. Additionally, we post-trained an earlier checkpoint, <a href="/news/introducing-inkling/#inkling-small">Inkling-Small (preview)</a>, in part using on-policy distillation with Inkling as the teacher. Starting from that checkpoint, we continued scaling agentic coding RL for two weeks. With these improvements, Inkling-Small surpassed Inkling on reasoning and agentic coding benchmarks. Inkling maintains an advantage on knowledge coverage and factuality.</p>
